    22	#        old task: north beam approaches the upper bar -> turns there in place
    23	#        combo:    north beam approaches the upper bar -> jumps to the lower bar's inner side ->
    24	#                  paints the reappearance square -> turns there using the legend
    25	#      The teleport breaks the local continuity of the old path, while the symmetric placement makes
    26	#      the pairing visible without hidden ordering.
    27	# b) Complexity calibration:
    28	#    - Only two obstacle colors are active in each instance, each shown twice. This is enough repeated
    29	#      evidence for portal pairing while keeping the color logic human-trackable.
    30	#    - The two active colors are forced to use opposite legend turns. Geometry is symmetric, but the
    31	#      output path family is not reducible to pure mirror symmetry because the horizontal and vertical
    32	#      portal pairs redirect differently.
    33	#    - Exactly one beam axis gets a second portal hit (north/south or east/west, chosen per sample).
    34	#      That keeps the variant visibly richer than "teleport once", but avoids tangled 3-hit loops.
    35	# c) Old assumptions that break:
    36	#    - Original hit handling assumed a color appears once and turning happens at the hit location.
